instruction that takes 4 cycles.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10593-1
02:08:53.887 --> 02:08:59.557
It could be an FMA or floating point
operation or some some instruction that

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10593-2
02:08:59.557 --> 02:09:04.565
has a fixed number of cycles.
So if we just have one warp in that's

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10593-3
02:09:04.565 --> 02:09:08.247
eligible,
then it's going to issue instruction in

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10593-4
02:09:08.247 --> 02:09:11.119
cycle 0, then it's going to be stalled.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10614-0
02:09:11.599 --> 02:09:15.584
for three cycles until that instruction
completes.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10614-1
02:09:15.584 --> 02:09:19.882
Then it'll be eligible again and it can
be reselected.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10614-2
02:09:19.882 --> 02:09:25.039
So we're going to basically have only 25%
utilization efficiency.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10667-0
02:09:28.639 --> 02:09:33.522
In the best case scenario in this very
simplistic and contrived example where

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10667-1
02:09:33.522 --> 02:09:36.526
the same instruction gets issued over and
over.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10667-2
02:09:36.526 --> 02:09:41.785
This does happen like within a tight loop,
but it's usually just a small subsection

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10667-3
02:09:41.785 --> 02:09:44.601
of code,
although it could go on for a long,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10667-4
02:09:44.601 --> 02:09:46.479
long time if it's a long loop.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10693-0
02:09:47.759 --> 02:09:53.061
So what we want is we want to be able to
fill these empty slots with other warps

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10693-1
02:09:53.061 --> 02:09:57.970
doing other things. So here's an example.
Now we instead of just one warp,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10693-2
02:09:57.970 --> 02:09:59.279
we now have 4 warps.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10732-0
02:10:00.319 --> 02:10:05.559
in this SMSP and they all do the same
four cycle instruction code,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10732-1
02:10:05.559 --> 02:10:11.737
but since they're initially, you know,
one will be selected in the first cycle

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10732-2
02:10:11.737 --> 02:10:16.585
and then it'll be stalled,
but the next one will be selected,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10732-3
02:10:16.585 --> 02:10:21.199
and then it will stall,
and the next one will be selected.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10770-0
02:10:21.439 --> 02:10:25.863
And since it's only a four-cycle
instruction,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10770-1
02:10:25.863 --> 02:10:33.267
we only need 4 warps to fill that up,
and then we can have 100% utilization.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10770-2
02:10:33.267 --> 02:10:40.479
It's your basic pipeline concept,
and now we get the latency fully hidden.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10779-0
02:10:40.639 --> 02:10:44.580
At the end,
we have instructions completing in full

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10779-1
02:10:44.580 --> 02:10:46.399
utilization every cycle.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10782-0
02:10:48.159 --> 02:10:49.999
Now, the reality is...

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10809-0
02:10:51.279 --> 02:10:56.081
Many instructions are a lot longer than 4
cycles. For instance,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10809-1
02:10:56.081 --> 02:11:02.309
memory latency can be hundreds of cycles.
Going out to global mem is generally 400

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10809-2
02:11:02.309 --> 02:11:03.359
to 600 cycles.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10816-0
02:11:05.199 --> 02:11:08.639
So we need lots more warps.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10857-0
02:11:10.719 --> 02:11:16.716
And we need more than just the ability
for one warp to execute one instruction,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10857-1
02:11:16.716 --> 02:11:20.539
then stall.
So we have this concept of instruction

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10857-2
02:11:20.539 --> 02:11:24.662
level parallelism,
which the compiler can optimize and

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10857-3
02:11:24.662 --> 02:11:29.759
allows us to actually have the warp,
for instance, issue of memory.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10893-0
02:11:30.239 --> 02:11:34.762
Access instruction,
and that instruction is non-blocking,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10893-1
02:11:34.762 --> 02:11:40.923
and then the code can continue and do
other operations that are independent of

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10893-2
02:11:40.923 --> 02:11:46.772
the result of that memory instruction,
while that instruction is executing

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10893-3
02:11:46.772 --> 02:11:48.799
asynchronously the memory.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10937-0
02:11:50.719 --> 02:11:53.790
you know,
the memory subsystem is going out,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10937-1
02:11:53.790 --> 02:11:56.929
fetching, retrieving the bits,
and meanwhile,

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10937-2
02:11:56.929 --> 02:12:02.321
other instructions which are independent
are continuing to execute within that

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10937-3
02:12:02.321 --> 02:12:05.460
warp.
And then also that same thing happening

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10937-4
02:12:05.460 --> 02:12:09.759
in the other warps,
so you end up with a lot more opportunity.

d9e392cf-61fd-4d98-9648-ab5dad3389bf/10942-0
02:12:09.839 --> 02:12:13.839
for parallelism to fill the stalled
cycles.

